# RFC 8288 Link headers — site-wide discovery pointers to resources that are
# genuinely the same on every page (sitemap, the RFC 9727 API catalog, the
# OpenAPI spec). Per-page pointers (e.g. an atom page's own markdown twin)
# are NOT here: Cloudflare Pages' _headers format can't template a per-path
# value into a header, and hand-writing one block per atom page (474 of
# them) would be an unmaintainable duplicate of the URL structure already
# expressed correctly in the sitemap and each page's own <head>. Those use a
# real <link rel="alternate"> tag instead — see generate_atom_pages.py.
/*
  Link: <https://a2uicatalog.ai/sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap", <https://a2uicatalog.ai/.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="service-desc"; type="application/linkset+json", <https://a2uicatalog.ai/openapi.json>; rel="service-desc"; type="application/json"

/
  Link: <https://a2uicatalog.ai/index.md>; rel="alternate"; type="text/markdown"
